  "notes": "Poses are changes on top of 'stance', in the fighter's own facing frame: x is the fighter's left, y is up, z is forward toward the opponent. pelvis {b} is measured from the fighter's spot on the mat. Feet {h} are points on the mat around that spot, so they stay planted when the hips move. Hands {hc} are offsets from the fighter's own upper chest. {j: 'opp.head', o: [...]} aims at the opponent's body, offset in the opponent's facing frame (their x is their left), so a strike reaches the target when in range and extends short of it when not. Both fighters stand orthodox (left foot forward). A strike's 'zone' is the side of the defender it threatens, from the defender's point of view. 'evade' maps head movement to a damage multiplier: 0 dodges it, 0.5 takes half, above 1 means moving into it; head movement not listed has no effect. 'track' strikes follow the target's head instead of aiming where it was (an uppercut finds a ducking head).",
